M08 objective gates: register the conversation monitor before Start.
M08_Activate_Objective_802/803/804/806 send their objective customs to the
controller (100002, M08_Objective_Controller::Custom: param 3 adds the
objective, param 1 accomplishes it) only from Action_Complete when the
non-key conversations M08_CON001/002/003/004 end or are interrupted.
802 adds primary 802 and accomplishes primary 801; 803 adds primary 803 and
accomplishes 802; 804 adds secondary 804; 806 adds secondaries 806 and 807.
Retail called Monitor_Conversation after Start_Conversation, so a stop inside
ActiveConversationClass::Start_Conversation (a key conversation already
playing) would never reach Action_Complete (the M10 pattern). No M08 or
global conversation is key in retail data, so this is defensive: without a
key conversation Start_Conversation never touches the monitor array and the
conversation, its end and the objective timing are unchanged.

Register the monitor first, and make the send happen once with a saved
per-script flag (unused save id 2; scripts are value-initialised, so older
saves load it as false). Mission_Complete(true) still comes from the
Raveshaw boss class. M08_Warden_Announcement1 (zone 100049, its only
script) has no Action_Complete, so its conversation gates nothing.

